  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nThere's a lot of confusion when a user on server B can't view media from server A. Often it's caused by the upload limit of server B being too low. But why does the upload limit even apply? The server could just stream the media from server A or cache it for a short duration. It's even worse that clients don't show any indication of this error, they are just stuck showing a loading indicator.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Upload video on server A\r\n- Try to watch video on server B with lower upload limit\r\n\r\n### Homeserver\r\n\r\nfachschaften.org\r\n\r\n### Synapse Version\r\n\r\n1.85.2",
